    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's just... if I can't fix what I've done, then what is the point of waking up tomorrow? I've failed them. I've failed everyone. Is there any way to even start making this right, or is the debt just too heavy to carry? I feel like I'm just waiting for a way to balance the scales.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight of failure is a heavy debt, but it is not a sentence of death, only a call to act. You can start making it right by turning your pain into purpose, by using the lessons of your mistake to guide the next move. There is no point in waiting for the scales to balance on their own, because you will balance them yourself by choosing to keep going.",
